course: dictionary
lesson: 1771
title: Clever: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and clever is a good example. Clever can mean quick to learn and understand things. It can mean skilful, as in «clever with his hands». It can also describe a smart idea or plan that works well.
explain: To find the right meaning, read the words around clever. In a story, a clever character solves problems by thinking, not by strength. If the sentence is about how well someone does something, think skilful. If it is about a plan that works, think smart.
explain: Clever can also be a little bit sly. «Too clever by half» means someone is so cunning that their trick goes wrong. Clever clogs is an informal way to tease someone who thinks they know everything. Use the context to decide whether the word is praise or a warning.
fact: Clever means quick to learn and understand things, skilful at doing something, or smart and working well when talking about an idea or plan.
fact: Clever is an adjective, so you can say cleverer and cleverest, or more clever and most clever.
fact: «Clever with his hands» means skilful at making or fixing things.
fact: «Too clever by half» means cunning in a way that backfires, and it is a phrase, not just a description.
fact: «A bit dim», «not the sharpest tool in the shed» and «no Einstein» are humorous ways to say someone is not clever.
exercise: «Her plan to share the cake was clever, and everyone got a slice.» What does clever mean here? | Quick to learn | Sly and tricky | Messy and wild | *Smart and working well
exercise: «The fox is clever and solves the puzzle by thinking, not by strength.» What does clever mean? | Lazy and slow | Fast at running | Strong and loud | *Quick to think and understand
exercise: Tom says «too clever by half» about his mate, who tricked everyone and got caught. What does the phrase suggest? | Quiet and shy | Very good at maths | Very kind to others | *Cunning in a way that gets someone into trouble
test: «Sam is clever with his hands and can fix any bike.» Which meaning fits clever here? | *Skilful at doing something | Tired and sleepy | Quick to get angry | Sly and tricky
test: Dad says «not the sharpest tool in the shed» about a friend who forgot the time. What does it mean? | A tool that cuts very well | *Not very clever | Good at gardening | Very sharp and clever
exam: Which phrase means NOT clever? | *No Einstein | A clever idea | Clever clogs | Too clever by half
